  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life-saving WASH and Nutrition services to drought-affected populations in Tigray, Amhara and Afar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the UNICEF project is to provide life-saving Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH) as well as Nutrition services to populations in Tigray, Amhara, affected by drought. UNICEF and its Implementing Partners rehabilitate, maintain, and expand existing water supply systems, including upgrading generator systems to solar power, alongside providing water storage facilities and WASH non-food items. Additionally, the program focuses on addressing the malnutrition crisis by identifying and treating moderate acute malnutrition (MAM) in children. Under this project, UNICEF will target a total of 119,664 people, including 32,340 women, 31,071 men, 28,679 girls, 27,554 boys, and 11,964 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
